TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"attempt":1,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/49","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-c","grep -n 'podman run' scripts/run-smoke.sh | grep -Eq -- ' (-i|--interactive|-a stdin)( |$)'"],"description":"The smoke script's podman invocation attaches stdin, so the heredoc program is delivered to the container instead of being discarded.","id":"heredoc-reaches-container"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"description":"scripts/run-smoke.sh executes the five probes in-container and exits 0.","id":"smoke-runs-and-passes"},{"argv":["python3","-c","import [redacted-token] d['status']=='pass',d;assert set(d['data'])>={'arch','fp8_cast','registry','aperture','admission'},d"],"description":"results/receipts/smoke.json exists with status pass and records all five probes.","id":"pass-receipt-present"},{"argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh && git diff --quiet && git diff --cached --quiet"],"description":"A second run over the already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, satisfying the checkpoint-purity contract.","id":"rerun-is-pure"},{"argv":["bash","-c","grep -n 'podman run' scripts/make-proxy.sh | grep -Eq -- ' (-i|--interactive|-a stdin)( |$)'"],"description":"scripts/make-proxy.sh's podman invocation also attaches stdin, so its heredoc is not silently discarded.","id":"proxy-builder-stdin-fixed"}],"dependencies":["cp-build"],"goal":"Make the container heredocs actually execute. In scripts/run-smoke.sh, add -i (or -a stdin) to the `podman run` invocation on line 10 so the `python3 -` heredoc body is delivered to the container; apply the same fix to the `podman run` invocation at scripts/make-proxy.sh:116, which has the identical silent-no-op defect. Add no other behavioral change: the five probes (arch, fp8_cast, registry, aperture, admission), the D12 failed/ quarantine, the receipt-restore purity guard, and the trailing validator all stay as written. After the fix, `bash scripts/run-smoke.sh` must run the probes in-container, print the receipt JSON, land results/receipts/smoke.json with status pass (or a fail receipt under results/receipts/failed/ if a probe genuinely fails), and exit 0; a second run over the already-correct base must leave every tracked file byte-identical per the checkpoint-purity note. Commit the receipt inside the lane commit so the later cp-smoke checkpoint re-run is a pure validator.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh","scripts/make-proxy.sh","results/receipts/smoke.json"]},"redacted":true,"retry":null,"taskId":"cp-smoke","verdict":"blocked"}
